---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_URL, ENTITY_STATEMENT } from '../data/site.js';

const websiteSchema = {
  '@type': 'WebSite',
  '@id': `${SITE_URL}/#website`,
  url: SITE_URL,
  name: 'AllyMadrone.com',
  description: ENTITY_STATEMENT,
  publisher: { '@id': `${SITE_URL}/#ally` }
};
---

<Base title="Home" path="/" extraSchema={websiteSchema}>
  <h1>Ally Madrone</h1>
  <p class="kicker">VP of Product at Deep Media · he/him</p>

  <p class="lede">
    I build AI systems that find digital harms before the victims have to. At
    <a href="https://deepmedia.ai">Deep Media</a>, a content security infrastructure company, I lead
    product for a platform that helps financial institutions, technology platforms, and government
    teams detect synthetic media, investigate fraud networks, and keep their communities safe. Deep
    Media's work is trusted by the U.S. Department of Defense and major technology platforms.
  </p>

  <p>
    Before this I spent a decade in identity and fraud, and before that I ran a horticultural
    research firm I founded and grew to a million dollars in annual revenue. The through line is the
    same question in every domain: how do we act with integrity toward the systems we're entangled
    with, whether they're ecological, digital, human, or artificial.
  </p>

  <p>
    Right now I'm focused on agentic AI for fraud investigation and trust and safety. Next up, I'm
    speaking at the IAFCI International Training Conference in Nashville on August 25, 2026.
  </p>

  <ul class="doors">
    <li>
      <a href="/experience">
        <strong>Work</strong>
        <span>Roles, dates, outcomes, and a machine-readable resume.</span>
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/writing">
        <strong>Writing</strong>
        <span>Essays and posts on content security, fraud, and AI governance.</span>
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/garden">
        <strong>Garden</strong>
        <span>Permaculture, woodworking, birds, and the rest of a whole life.</span>
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Booking a talk? Start at <a href="/speaking">speaking</a>. Everything else goes through
    <a href="/contact">contact</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    Want a site like this one? I built it in a sitting with Claude and I like helping other people
    own the answer to their own name. The how, and the prompt, are on
    <a href="/own-your-name">own your name</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
